descriptionByLocale.en:
The Rorschach-Rheintal BZR vocational and further education centre is an important commercial and industrial cantonal centre of competence in eastern Switzerland. At the Rorschach and Altstätten sites, around 1,900 students from different cantons and nations are accompanied in their basic vocational education. The BZR combines sound vocational training, contemporary learning forms, high practical proximity and close cooperation with teaching companies, professional associations and other educational partners. The professional further education (WZR) completes our educational offer.

In a variety of courses and courses, around 2,000 professionals expand their qualifications annually.

What awaits you: As the Rector, you bear the overall responsibility for the strategic, pedagogical, personnel, financial and organizational management of the Rorschach-Rheintal vocational and continuing education centre. In addition, you take over a small teaching pool according to cantonal requirements and thus remain close to the school's core business.

• lead the school management clearly, participatively and developmentally oriented;
• manage the further development and implementation of the school strategy in the sense of the vision BZR30+ based on the cantonal vocational training strategy;
• strengthen the quality of teaching, school development and innovation capacity of the BZR;
• shape a culture of trust, responsibility, commitment and cooperation;
• represent the BZR in and outside credible, networked and convincing;
• maintain cooperation with the teaching establishments, professional associations and partner institutions as well as the Office for Vocational Training,

• position the BZR as a performance and connection-oriented and forward-looking cantonal competence centre of vocational education and training.

What distinguishes you: For this responsible leadership task, you bring joy to people, education and development as well as a high level of identification with vocational education and training.

• a knowledge of the Swiss vocational training system and a good understanding of political, economic and social contexts;
• a pedagogical qualification for upper secondary education or equivalent training, as well as a completed school management training or the willingness to complete it in a part-time manner;
• experience in strategy, organisational or organisational skills;
• experience in the field of vocational training and the development of vocational training;
